{"id":226241859345078,"type":"album","name":"Trespass","artist":"Genesis","year":1970,"weight":17,"info":{"cover":"https://dn711308.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-f0e2a5a8-861f-48d2-8900-2c8ce23444e7/mbid-f0e2a5a8-861f-48d2-8900-2c8ce23444e7-34155611438.jpg","kind":"Album","tracks":6,"country":"JP","scaruffi":7.0,"yt":"8ljNXAdX7Vc","links":{"spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/album/17hKeFpIov0cxAFQbGegEy","youtube":"https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=OLAK5uy_nEkpELGC5uebWiH3Jo0Q6hadV_IeVAGkA","rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/genesis/trespass"},"desc":"Trespass is the second studio album by Genesis and was recorded and released in 1970. The only album with drummer John Mayhew and the last with guitarist Anthony Phillips, Trespass had a folk-flavoured progressive rock sound that was a marked departure from their earlier work, and foreshadowed the path the band would follow through the 1970s. The compositions were generally much longer and complex than before, featuring several different musical sections. The sound evokes a kind of 'pastoral English idyll' espoused by numerous progressive rock bands of the time. To this end, much use is made of multi-tracked 12-string acoustic ."},"artist_ref":{"id":91958884229881,"name":"Genesis","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/2180_-_Pittsburgh_-_Mellon_Arena_-_Genesis_-_The_Carpet_Crawlers.JPG?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":18872195504512,"type":"genre","name":"Pop Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":740,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":191826593279813,"type":"genre","name":"Art Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":531,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":138197775829889,"type":"genre","name":"Progressive Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":439,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":65887344945565,"type":"genre","name":"Symphonic Prog","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":210,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":117566163487916,"type":"genre","name":"Progre